ion_affine_transformation_and_linearity_016","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"Which function has the displayed affine form?","options":["$f(x,y)=xy+1$","$f(x,y)=2^x+y$","$f(x,y)=3x-y+2$","$f(x,y)=\\sin x$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"7e34fb08c0b1645c76382da6","time_limit":20},{"id":"expansion_affine_transformation_and_linearity_018","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"Let $f(x,y)=x-4y+6$. If $y$ increases by $c$ while $x$ is fixed, how does $f$ change?","options":["It changes by $c$.","It changes by exactly $6c$.","It does not change.","It changes by $-4c$."],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"3d8c5372ebcfb4ed4d354118","time_limit":30},{"id":"expansion_affine_transformation_and_linearity_020","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"Let $\\boldsymbol{A}=\\begin{pmatrix}2&1\\end{pmatrix}$, $\\boldsymbol{b}=-3$, and $\\boldsymbol{x}=(4,5)$. What is $\\boldsymbol{A}\\boldsymbol{x}+\\boldsymbol{b}$?","options":["$13$","$10$","$5$","$16$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"df21b55ccb7162e5d1e479a8","time_limit":30},{"id":"year_1_2a_math_iii_analysis_affine_transformation_and_linearity_1de39c43_003_curated20261027_001","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"Consider $f(x,y)=x+2y-1$ on $\\mathbb{R}^2$. In the terminology of this wiki, which description is correct?","options":["Affine but not linear, since $f(0,0)=-1\\ne0$.","Both linear and affine, since each variable appears to the first power.","Linear but not affine, since it has a constant term.","Neither linear nor affine, since it has a constant term."],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"c547c572924601920bdffe7d","time_limit":30},{"id":"year_1_2a_math_iii_analysis_affine_transformation_and_linearity_1de39c43_004_curated20261027_002","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"Which of the following functions on $\\mathbb{R}^2$ is not affine?","options":["$g(x,y)=x+xy$","$f(x,y)=x+2y-1$","$q(x,y)=x-y$","$c(x,y)=5$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"c0cb72316c018940ab6523dd","time_limit":20},{"id":"year_1_2a_math_iii_analysis_affine_transformation_and_linearity_1de39c43_006_curated20261027_003","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Let $f(\\boldsymbol{x})=a_1x_1+\\cdots+a_nx_n+b$ be an affine function on $\\mathbb{R}^n$. What is its graph $\\{(\\boldsymbol{x},f(\\boldsymbol{x}))\\colon\\boldsymbol{x}\\in\\mathbb{R}^n\\}$?","options":["An affine hyperplane of $\\mathbb{R}^{n+1}$, through the origin exactly when $b=0$.","A hyperplane of $\\mathbb{R}^n$, namely the level set where $f$ takes the value $b$.","A line in $\\mathbb{R}^{n+1}$, for every $n$.","A linear subspace of $\\mathbb{R}^{n+1}$, for every value of $b$."],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"9df062e562b3ee4f421443e1","time_limit":40},{"id":"year_1_2a_math_iii_analysis_affine_transformation_and_linearity_1de39c43_012_curated20261027_004","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"Let $\\boldsymbol{A}=\\begin{pmatrix}1&0\\\\0&2\\end{pmatrix}$, $\\boldsymbol{b}=(3,-1)$ and $\\boldsymbol{x}=(2,4)$. What is $\\boldsymbol{A}\\boldsymbol{x}+\\boldsymbol{b}$?","options":["$(2,8)$","$(3,-1)$","$(8,5)$","$(5,7)$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"bb002db5a8c6f0416e1c7f6b","time_limit":30},{"id":"expansion_affine_transformation_and_linearity_013_curated20261027_005","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Let $\\boldsymbol{f}(\\boldsymbol{x})=\\boldsymbol{A}\\boldsymbol{x}+\\boldsymbol{b}$ be an affine map from $\\mathbb{R}^n$ to $\\mathbb{R}^k$. How can the shift vector $\\boldsymbol{b}$ be read off from the values of $\\boldsymbol{f}$?","options":["$\\boldsymbol{b}=\\boldsymbol{f}(\\boldsymbol{0})$","$\\boldsymbol{b}=\\boldsymbol{f}(\\boldsymbol{e}_1)$, the value at the first standard basis vector","$\\boldsymbol{b}=\\boldsymbol{f}(\\boldsymbol{x})-\\boldsy